AB  - Artificial general intelligence (AGI) is poised to revolutionize multiple aspects of human life, offering unprecedented capabilities for problem-solving, decision-making, and autonomous learning. However, its influence on misinformation remains a critical issue. On the one hand, AGI offers advanced capabilities for combating misinformation, including real-time detection, cognitive inoculation, and automated fact-checking. On the other hand, AGI poses significant risks, such as generating highly sophisticated disinformation, enabling hyperpersonalized propaganda, and exacerbating existing information crises. This paper critically examines AGI’s dual role in the misinformation ecosystem, highlighting its potential as both a powerful tool for mitigation and a source of new threats. Ethical, technical, and governance implications are explored, with actionable recommendations for proactive policy and regulatory frameworks to ensure responsible deployment.
