AB  - The artificial intelligence (AI) revolution is surrounded by abysses of risks. These include problems of AI automation, general AI or super AI, and manipulation of reality, such as deepfakes, and eventually a possible collapse of truth. An essential conundrum is how to align AI with sound ethics or our intentions, the so-called alignment problem. The long-term effects of advanced AI models, when they are exposed to reality and other AI models, are notoriously hard to predict. Understanding the mathematical and computer science basis of AI and thus the root causes of this uncertainty is essential to mitigate these risks. The ability to dissect or unbox the ‘black boxes’ of AI leads to increased transparency and in-depth understanding. This is instrumental in the wise governance of the ideal AI.
