AB  - This review presents a comprehensive analysis of machine learning (ML) applications in agriculture, with a particular emphasis on the increasing role of data fusion and advanced AI techniques in precision farming. It addresses a notable gap in existing surveys by providing an in-depth examination of the transition from traditional ML approaches to modern techniques, offering a cohesive synthesis of their evolution and impact. Structured around four key research objectives (RO-1 to RO-4), the study explores ML integration across pre-harvest, harvest, and post-harvest stages; demonstrates the benefits of multi-source data fusion, including remote sensing, IoT, and biological data for ML models; examines current research trends; and compiles essential public datasets to support future model development. The paper highlights the use of emerging methods, such as transformers, GANs, federated learning, continual learning, and explainable AI, in addressing modern agricultural challenges. Furthermore, the paper outlines challenges such as data heterogeneity, privacy, and infrastructure gaps, and proposes future research directions to guide sustainable and inclusive agricultural innovation.
