AB  - Undoubtedly, Generative AI (GenAI) and, in particular, language models are expected to play a pivotal role in the design and operation of communications and networking systems. By exploiting multimodal contextual information using the attention mechanism called Transformers, the door is opened to a variety of use cases such as intent-based networking (IBN), log anomaly detection, multi-sensory mobility management, and multi-agent conversation. The inner dynamics of Transformers require yet explainable AI tools to characterize the confidence of their outputs, among other metrics. This chapter delves into the potential of GenAI for telecommunications, while classifying its vulnerabilities. A use case is then presented, where a small Generative Pre-trained Transformer (GPT) language model plays the role of an interpreter, translating the emerging messages in multi-agent communication. Various XAI metrics are finally invoked to verify the confidence of the GPT-augmented agents.
