AB  - With the rapid development of vehicle intelligence and Internet connection technology, various network attacks threaten driving safety. IoV intrusion detection has become crucial. However, previous studies have primarily relied on local spatial features and local temporal correlations of message sequences for intrusion detection, without fully considering global features. Meanwhile, IoV requires lightweight detection mechanisms due to the real-time and fast characteristics. Existing inaccurate and inefficient intrusion detection makes IoV vulnerable to undetected attacks. To extract global features for intrusion detection, this paper proposes an IoV intrusion detection method using Global spatio-temporal Representations (IoVGR), which broadens the scope of analysis using attention mechanisms and applies adaptive feature fusion to extract global representations. Furthermore, to achieve lightweight detection, this paper adopts multiple knowledge distillation (MKD), which introduces teacher assistant models and intermediate layer mapping to compress the detection model. We conduct extensive experimental evaluations on the VeReMi Extension dataset, which show that the average F1-score of multi-classification and bi-classification attack detection for IoVGR are higher than the best baseline method by 2.31% and 4.16%, respectively. The compressed IoV intrusion detection model reduces the number of parameters by 93.92% and the amount of calculation by 99.44% while ensuring accuracy. Moreover, IoVGR is executed on the UNSW-NB15 dataset and the ORACLE RF fingerprint dataset with an improved F1-score of 1.22% and 3.81%, demonstrating the universality of the model.
