AB  - Artificial Intelligence (AI) transforms medical learning through the implementation of modern educational and learning approaches that develop novel teaching, learning, assessment methods, and training programs. AI uses educational data analysis to develop personalized learning materials that match the learning needs of medical students. AI systems create customized learning experiences for medical students and trainees through their system that provides personalized feedback together with specific assessment results and tailored learning routes that build knowledge, skills, and clinical expertise. AI technology develops intelligent tutoring systems that support medical students in learning through their medical training in complex clinical situations. AI technology evaluates how students answer questions to determine their knowledge deficiencies, which results in feedback that enhances their clinical reasoning and decision-making skills. The grading process becomes automatic for medical educators through AI technology, which also monitors student learning development and identifies areas needing additional specific instructions. Medical students use AI simulators along with virtual patients to perform clinical tasks, make treatment plans, and develop communication abilities and clinical judgment. AI technologies deliver training programs with smart evaluation systems and transform how medical practitioners learn and develop their skills. The implementation of AI in medical education leads to improved learning outcomes, which enable better healthcare delivery and patient results.
