AB  - This chapter presents the field of study of adversarial machine learning and how it impacts the Internet of Things (IoT) paradigm. It begins with an introduction to Machine Learning (ML) techniques and how these apply to the design of intrusion detection systems for securing the IoT paradigm. We then present contributions in the domain of anomaly detectors (intrusion detector family) for Industrial Control Systems (ICS) and also provide a comprehensive explanation of adversarial machine learning for an ICS. We provide an illustration of research gaps associated with ICS attack models in general and adversarial ML attacks in particular. The literature review was conducted through an exhaustive search of the terms “Adversarial Learning”, “Anomaly Detection”, “Industrial Control Systems”, and “ICS”. The search engines utilized in this research comprises; Google Scholar, ACM, IEEE, Springer, and Elsevier.
