AB  - This chapter provides a comprehensive overview of the foundational principles, methodologies, and transformative roles of Artificial Intelligence (AI) in modern energy systems. As global energy infrastructures shift toward decarbonization, decentralization, and digitalization, AI emerges as a critical enabler, offering data-driven solutions to manage complexity, optimize performance, and enhance system resilience. The chapter explores key AI paradigms, including machine learning, deep learning, and generative AI, and discusses their applications across forecasting, grid control, demand response, and asset management. It highlights how AI supports integrating renewable energy, coordinating distributed resources, and real-time decision-making in digitalized energy system operations. The chapter also addresses crucial challenges in applying AI in safety systems. Finally, it underscores the imperative for robust governance frameworks and standards to ensure the safe, transparent, and ethical deployment of AI technologies within critical energy infrastructure.
