AB  - Blockchain technology has emerged as an innovation capable of transforming various fields and industries. Although initially popularized by cryptocurrencies, blockchain is now being utilized in various areas. This generates increased interest in its integration with other popular technologies, particularly machine learning (ML). ML is a powerful tool that has demonstrated its efficacy in solving a wide range of practical problems by leveraging the ever-increasing amount of data across many business domains. However, as ML is used in increasingly complex real-world problems with huge volumes of data, new challenges such as data security and privacy have arisen. By leveraging key features of blockchain, ML would benefit from the implementation of secure, private, and decentralized systems that promote better data and model sharing. In this chapter, we first provide an overview of basic blockchain and ML concepts. We then examine the integration and impact of blockchain on ML techniques, and analyze how such a combination can benefit various industries and businesses, for example, healthcare, transportation, education, etc. We conclude by discussing the key advantages of integrating blockchain into ML, and then highlight the potential issues and challenges associated with this integration for future work.
